s=item('lem-cm-piecewise-c1-jump-derivative');s=s.replace('deps: [','deps: [cor-mean-value-theorem, ',1).replace('dependency_roles:\n','dependency_roles:\n  cor-mean-value-theorem: mathematical-premise\n',1)
a=s.index('1.1 Local integrability:');z=s.index('For Borel measurability',a);s=s[:a]+r'''1.1 Local integrability: let $K\subseteq I$ be compact. If $K=\varnothing$, its integral is zero. Otherwise choose $c<t_*<d$ with $K\cup\{t_*\}\subset(c,d)$ and $[c,d]\subset I$; this is possible because $K\cup\{t_*\}$ is compact in the open interval $I$. Define $q:[c,d]\to\mathbb R$ by $q(t)=p(t)$ for $t\ne t_*$ and $q(t_*)=p(t_*^-)$. It is bounded by continuity on the two sides and the finite one-sided limits. '''+s[z:]
