s=item('thm-cm-work-energy-balance');s=s.replace('let $U:I\\times Q\\to\\mathbb R$ be continuously differentiable, i.e. of class $C^1$ on the open set $I\\times Q$','let $U:I\\times Q\\to\\mathbb R$ be the restriction of a function $\\widehat U:J\\times Q\\to\\mathbb R$ of class $C^1$, where $J\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ is an open interval containing $I$');s=s.replace('let $\\partial_tU$ be the partial derivative in the time variable.','let $\\partial_tU$ and the spatial derivatives on $I\\times Q$ denote the derivatives of $\\widehat U$ restricted there. At an included endpoint of $I$, derivatives of curves are limits relative to $I$ (one-sided there); this preserves closed and half-open time intervals.');s=s.replace('a $C^1$ function $U:I\\times Q\\to\\mathbb R$','a function $U:I\\times Q\\to\\mathbb R$ with the stated $C^1$ extension $\\widehat U$ to $J\\times Q$');s=s.replace('Since $U$ is $C^1$ and $\\gamma(t)\\in I\\times Q$ for all $t$, [L2] gives $D(U\\circ\\gamma)(t)=DU(\\gamma(t))\\circ\\gamma\'(t)$','Since $\\widehat U$ is $C^1$ on the open neighborhood $J\\times Q$ of $\\gamma(I)$, [L2] gives the usual chain rule at interior points. At an included endpoint, $\\gamma(t+h)=\\gamma(t)+h\\gamma\'(t)+o(h)$ as $h\\to0$ relative to $I$, and total differentiability gives $\\widehat U(\\gamma(t)+v)=\\widehat U(\\gamma(t))+D\\widehat U(\\gamma(t))v+o(|v|)$. Substituting the first expansion into the second proves the same relative derivative there. Thus $(U\\circ\\gamma)\'(t)=D\\widehat U(\\gamma(t))\\gamma\'(t)$');write('items/thm-cm-work-energy-balance.md',s)
